---
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import { HOME } from "@consts";
import { url } from "@lib/utils";
---

<PageLayout title={HOME.TITLE} description={HOME.DESCRIPTION}>
  <Container>
    <h1 class="animate font-semibold text-black dark:text-white text-3xl">
      Earth, Wind, Water - Wire
    </h1>
    <p class="animate">A narrative atlas of data centres on the island of Ireland</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">About</h2>
      <p>
        In 2025, data centres used 23% of Ireland's metered electricity, up
        from 5% in 2015 (Central Statistics Office). Most of them sit around
        Dublin, where the grid is under strain. Meanwhile, in the west and
        north, wind farms are switched off because the lines cannot carry
        their power.
      </p>
      <p>
        This atlas follows data centres through the land, power and water
        they draw on. It maps where they are, how they connect to the grid,
        where they are contested and where clean power is being wasted. It
        argues for a grid that reaches the whole country, so that new
        development can use all of the renewable power the island makes.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={url("contested_grounds")}><b>Read the story</b></a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Chapters</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li><b>Wired In:</b> the substations and high-voltage lines that serve the sites.</li>
        <li><b>Extraction:</b> sites with permits to burn fuel on site.</li>
        <li><b>Contest:</b> which sites were contested, and why.</li>
        <li><b>Alternative Benefits:</b> Tallaght, where data centre waste heat warms public buildings.</li>
        <li><b>Wasted Wind:</b> wind power turned down in the west, north and across the border.</li>
        <li><b>Grow:</b> a grid built to use 100% of renewable power.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">Data</h2>
      <p>
        Central Statistics Office; Environmental Protection Agency
        (greenhouse gas permits); EirGrid and SONI (curtailment reports and
        grid planning); Government of Ireland (Climate Action Plan 2025);
        Atlas of Data Center Politics; South Dublin County Council;
        OpenStreetMap contributors. Full sources are listed at the end of
        the story.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm">
        Made for GIS for Design Practices, Columbia GSAPP, Fall 2026. Built
        with the course's <a href="https://github.com/design-practices/astro-maplibre-template">Astro maplibre template</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</PageLayout>
